    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.06_topology_jepa.chapters.05_vjepa_temporal_extension.sections.01_spatiotemporal_patch_category.concrete_anchor#tailpatch" .
silm:instances_papers_06_topology_jepa_chapters_05_vjepa_temporal_extension_sections_01_spatiotemporal_patch_category_concrete_anchor#tailpatch silm:hasLongDescription "The TailPatch is the rectangular pixel window covering the tail of Mittens including the 28cm length tag and the white-tuft marking. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'U_tail', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
silm:instances_papers_06_topology_jepa_chapters_05_vjepa_temporal_extension_sections_01_spatiotemporal_patch_category_concrete_anchor#overlapzone a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.06_topology_jepa.chapters.05_vjepa_temporal_extension.sections.01_spatiotemporal_patch_category.concrete_anchor#overlapzone" .
silm:instances_papers_06_topology_jepa_chapters_05_vjepa_temporal_extension_sections_01_spatiotemporal_patch_category_concrete_anchor#overlapzone silm:hasLongDescription "The OverlapZone is the shared pixel region where the head patch and body patch both cover the neck-joint region of Mittens, requiring agreement on the apex glyph. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'U_overlap', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
