silm:instances_papers_06_topology_jepa_chapters_05_vjepa_temporal_extension_sections_01_spatiotemporal_patch_category_concrete_anchor#headlocalhypothesis silm:hasLongDescription "The HeadLocalHypothesis is the local olog hypothesis for the head patch: cat-classification node plus outgoing Cat morphism, signed by Dr. Osei in the May 2026 Tartu Animal Clinic record. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'D_head', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
