silm:instances_papers_06_topology_jepa_chapters_05_vjepa_temporal_extension_sections_01_spatiotemporal_patch_category_concrete_anchor#bodylocalhypothesis silm:hasLongDescription "The BodyLocalHypothesis is the local olog hypothesis for the body patch: BodyMass:4.2kg quality node plus the typed measurement arrow from scale-witness WeightMeas to Mittens. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'D_body', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
